  "description": "Floor Area C. 176 sq m / 1894 sq ft\n\nFlynn Estate Agents are delighted to present No. 158 Georgian Village to the market for sale. This beautifully presented five-bedroom detached family home offers elegant, light-filled and generously proportioned accommodation throughout and enjoys a quiet position within the highly sought-after Georgian Village development. Recently refurbished, the property has been thoughtfully enhanced with premium flooring throughout, a stylish new guest W.C., a refreshed contemporary kitchen complete with brand new integrated appliances and a newly fitted utility room. In addition, the property offers excellent potential to further extend (subject to the necessary planning permission), providing purchasers with the opportunity to create their ideal forever home.\nThe well-appointed accommodation briefly comprises an inviting entrance porch, a spacious entrance hall, guest cloakroom, an elegant living room with double doors opening to a generous dining room. The spacious kitchen/breakfast room forms the heart of the home and is complemented by a separate family room to the front. A door from the kitchen leads to the newly fitted utility room, which in turn provides internal access to the attached garage.\nUpstairs, there are five generously proportioned bedrooms, including a superb principal bedroom with en-suite shower room, together with a well-appointed family bathroom. Outside, the private rear garden is predominantly laid in lawn and has been thoughtfully designed to maximise the outdoor space. A sunken patio provides a wonderful setting for outdoor seating and relaxation, while a bespoke outdoor kitchen features a stainless steel preparation area, sink and barbecue. Mature trees and established hedging provide an excellent degree of privacy, while a powered concrete garden shed and dual side access further enhance the practicality of this impressive outdoor space. To the front, a private driveway provides off-street parking for two cars. \n\nThe Georgian Village is one of Castleknock`s most established and sought-after residential developments, superbly positioned between the vibrant Castleknock Village and the magnificent Phoenix Park. Residents enjoy the convenience of pedestrian access to Castleknock Road, College Road and the picturesque Whites Road, providing a pleasant walk directly into the Phoenix Park.\nThe area is exceptionally well served by an excellent selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools, many of which are within comfortable walking distance. A wealth of recreational and sporting amenities are also close at hand, including GAA, rugby and football clubs, Castleknock Tennis Club, several renowned golf clubs, scenic walks through the Phoenix Park, together with an excellent choice of cafés, restaurants, boutiques and everyday conveniences in nearby Castleknock Village. Viewing is highly recommended.\n\nEntrance Porch - 2.39m (7'10\") x 1.82m (6'0\")\nTiled floor, recessed lighting\n\nEntrance Hall - 7.56m (24'10\") x 1.8m (5'11\")\nStylish ash-toned wood effect laminate flooring, coving and cornicing detail, understairs storage, pendant lighting\n\nLounge - 4.99m (16'4\") x 3.83m (12'7\")\nFlooring laid in carpet, feature gas fireplace with marble surround, cornicing and coving detail, pendant lighting, double doors through to family room\n\nFamily Room - 3.83m (12'7\") x 4.49m (14'9\")\nflooring laid in carpet, cornicing and coving detail, overlooking rear garden\n\nStudy / Play room - 2.74m (9'0\") x 4.34m (14'3\")\nHigh quality ash effect wood floor laminate, access to kitchen, overlooking front garden\n\nGuest W.C - 1.92m (6'4\") x 1.79m (5'10\")\nNewly fitted, wood floor laminate, w.c, wash hand basin\n\nKitchen - 5.11m (16'9\") x 5.16m (16'11\")\nBright and spacious fitted kitchen with ample floor and wall units, brand new appliances including integrated Lamona double oven, Beko dishwasher, Zanussi hob, recessed lighting and pendant lighting, sliding door access to rear garden\n\nUtility - 2.46m (8'1\") x 2.24m (7'4\")\nNewly fitted worktop and units, sink, storage, washing machine, access to garage\n\nLanding - 4.21m (13'10\") x 3.5m (11'6\")\nFlooring laid in carpet, large hotpress, attic with Stira access, elegant wall sconce\n\nPrimary Bedroom - 4.24m (13'11\") x 4.2m (13'9\")\nFlooring laid in carpet, Georgian style double glazed windows overlooking front garden\n\nEnsuite - 2.85m (9'4\") x 0.87m (2'10\")\nLino floor covering, tiled, w.c, wash hand basin, shower\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.38m (14'4\") x 2.74m (9'0\")\nFlooring laid in carpet, spacious double bedroom overlooking front garden\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.81m (9'3\") x 3.03m (9'11\")\nFlooring laid in carpet, overlooking rear garden\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.16m (10'4\") x 2.47m (8'1\")\nFlooring laid in carpet, overlooking rear garden\n\nBedroom 5 - 2.45m (8'0\") x 2.52m (8'3\")\nFlooring laid in carpet, overlooking rear garden\n\nBathroom\nLino floor covering, w.c, wash hand basin, bath and separate shower,\n\nGarage - 3.42m (11'3\") x 2.27m (7'5\")\nStorage",
